      "options": { "code": { "language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false }, "content": "### Storage lifetime notes\n\n- **microSD:** consumer SD cards generally do not expose a standardized remaining-life or write-endurance counter. This dashboard therefore tracks root filesystem capacity, write/read trend, and I/O pressure as early-warning signals.\n- **External SSD:** SMART is available and will be added as a separate, low-frequency probe. SMART results and all Prometheus data are stored on `/mnt/data`, not on the microSD.\n- node_exporter reads kernel counters; its one-minute scrape does not itself write to the microSD.", "mode": "markdown" },
      "pluginVersion": "13.2.2",
      "title": "About storage monitoring",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
