      "id": 18,
      "options": { "code": { "language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false }, "content": "### SMART and lifetime interpretation\n\n- SMART health and error counters are **indicators**, not a guaranteed failure forecast. A drive can fail suddenly due to controller, USB, power, or other physical faults even when these values are normal. Keep backups of important data.\n- **Available reserved space** is a vendor-reported SMART value. It is not displayed as a predicted remaining lifetime.\n- **Total LBAs written (raw)** has an unverified vendor unit on this model, so it is retained only as a trend counter and is not converted to TB/TBW.\n- The SMART probe reads attributes once per day and does not start a self-test. A lifetime estimate, if ever added, must be explicitly marked as a prediction with its assumptions.", "mode": "markdown" },
      "pluginVersion": "13.2.2",
      "title": "About SSD SMART monitoring",
      "type": "text"
    }
